EQBar is a ground-up rewrite inspired by eqMac:
  eqMac — https://github.com/bitgapp/eqMac
  Copyright (c) Roman Kisil (Nodeful) / Bitgapp Ltd.
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  EQBar re-implements eqMac's feature set (Basic / Advanced / Expert EQ, volume boost and balance,
  per-app volume, Audio Unit hosting, spatial rooms, AutoEQ integration) and reads eqMac's exported
  preset format. No eqMac source code is included.

Headphone correction profiles are downloaded at runtime from AutoEq:
  AutoEq — https://github.com/jaakkopasanen/AutoEq
  Copyright (c) 2018-2022 Jaakko Pasanen. Licensed under the MIT License.
  EQBar does not bundle AutoEq data.

Algorithms:
  Biquad filters follow Robert Bristow-Johnson's "Audio EQ Cookbook".
  Crossfeed follows Boris Mikhaylov's bs2b (Bauer stereophonic-to-binaural) design.
  Spatial rendering uses Apple's AUSpatialMixer system component.
